<tr><td>4096</td><td>125.3</td><td>595.4</td><td>338.3</td><td>256</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="bench-note">Both runtimes share each actor's state instead of copying it, so snapshot cost follows the number of actors, not their size. A glowcap snapshot takes 16.2 µs with 64-byte actors and 29 µs with 16384-byte actors. The runtimes differ, so compare their trends, not their absolute times. On restore, glowcap frees rewound copies immediately, and Goblins leaves that cleanup to its garbage collector.</p>
